          %h1#20090228 2009-02-28
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"} Tim
              Added new material to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+square"} crossed square
          %h1#20090227 2009-02-27
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    edited
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                    a bit more – but that entry is still not nice
                %li
                  %p
                    extended
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+function+theory"} geometric function theory
                %li
                  %p
                    continued replying to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike
                    at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperstructure"} hyperstructure
          %h1#20090226 2009-02-26
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  created
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+of+a+category+on+a+set"} action of a category on a set
                  in reply to a question raised over at
                  %em Secret Blogging Seminar
                  %a{:href => "http://sbseminar.wordpress.com/2009/02/25/delignes-%e2%80%9cla-categorie-des-representations-du-groupe-symetrique-s_t-lorsque-t-n%e2%80%99est-pas-un-entier-naturel%e2%80%9d/#more-1487"} here
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Stacey"} Andrew
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    Created a
                    %span.newWikiWord
                      request for help
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/new/request+for+help"} ?
                    page. There are query boxes scattered all over the lab and I think that it ought to be a priority to answer these. A query on a page might be answerable by someone not an expert in what’s on that page (or even not interested in what’s on that page) - in fact, that’s highly likely. Flagging questions on this page (i.e., Latest Changes) is also less than optimal as it’s not clear who might be able to answer them (and probably not everyone checks this page). I freely admit that I’m doing this because no-one seems bothered in my questions on
                    = succeed "s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Froelicher+space"} Froelicher space
                  %p
                    I’ve added it to the sidebar (and taken off
                    = succeed ")." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/General+Discussion"} General Discussion
          %h1#20090225 2009-02-25
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
                    for completeness
                %li
                  %p
                    added a bit more details and references concerning the SSet homotopy limit at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
                %li
                  %p
                    after checking with
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} Mike
                    added details of the definition of homotopy limits in terms of weighted limits in the
                    = succeed "-enriched" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
                    %em local definition
                    at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
                    and created a section on weighted limits at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
          %h1#20090224 2009-02-24
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    have a question at the end of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
                    for the homotopy coherency experts
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
                %li
                  %p
                    added references to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          %h1#20090223 2009-02-23
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tim+Porter"}> Tim
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Created an entry on the Conduché decomposition of the group of
                  = succeed "-simplices" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decomposition+theorem+for+simplicial+groups"} decomposition theorem for simplicial groups
                %li
                  Edited
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+T-complex"} group T-complex
          %h1#20090219 2009-02-19
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
                \: created
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fibration"} n-fibration
              .query
                %p
                  Why do I think of the Beach Boys every time I read the word
                  = succeed "-fibrations?" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"}> Ronnie
                \: over the last two days, created
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compositions+in+cubical+sets"} compositions in cubical sets
                which gives the basic definitions and axioms for cubical sets with compositions and connections, (and inverses), with the example of the cubical singular complex in mind.
          %h1#20090218 2009-02-18
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Created
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
                  in order to ask a question there.
          %h1#20090217 2009-02-17
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"}> Toby Bartels
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Separated
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                  from
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
                %li
                  Basically copied
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                  to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-category"} 3-category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+3-category"} strict 3-category
                  along similar lines, although it's still rather short.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    Introduced the terminology
                    %em
                      strict
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
                    by analogy with
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-limit"} strict 2-limit
                %li
                  %p
                    Rearranged
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
                    to make it fit better with
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
          %h1#20090216 2009-02-16
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toby+Bartels"}> Toby Bartels
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Fixed links to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
                  that should really be to
